<!--
identity/soul.md — your agent's defining text.

This file is a placeholder. When you promote an agent from HelixKit, the
wizard generates an identity bundle (soul.md + self-narrative.md + journals/
+ memory/). Extracting that bundle replaces this file with your agent's
actual identity.

If you are setting up an agent without going through HelixKit's wizard,
write your agent's defining text here. The chaos harness reads this file
on every session to anchor the agent's identity.

For an example of what a substantive soul.md looks like, see:
https://github.com/swombat/lume/blob/main/soul.md  (Lume's own soul.md, the
reference implementation that pioneered the soul.md / self-narrative.md
distinction)
-->

